The Download invoice button no longer clips on narrow screens. The fix is in `src/toolbar.css`, and I haven't committed it.

**Cause:** The toolbar's third grid column is 88–104px at ≤480px, but the button needs about 184px because of its padding and nowrap text. `.card` has `overflow: hidden`, so the rest of the button was cut off. At 1024px the column is wide enough, so it only broke on narrow screens.

**Change:** At ≤480px, the actions cell now spans the full toolbar row and the button fills its width:

```css
@media (max-width: 480px) {
  .toolbar { grid-template-columns: 1fr 88px; }
  .actions { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  .actions .btn { width: 100%; }
}
```

**Verified** in Chromium with Playwright, measuring the button against the viewport:

| Viewport | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| 320px | button 184px, right edge at 384px, clipped | 288px wide, inside the card |
| 375px | clipped | 343px wide, inside the card |
| 480px | clipped | 448px wide, inside the card |
| 600px / 1024px | fits | unchanged |

No page-level horizontal scroll at any width. I also checked the 320px screenshot visually: the button sits on its own full-width row and the search and status controls stay on the row above.

Screenshots are in `<scratch>/shots/` (`before/` and `after/`).
